I lean over, eyes dart to the life-giving parts, </verse-line><verse-line>run the protocol, place the lines.</verse-line></verse-group><verse-group><verse-line>In death-giving trauma, the mind goes </verse-line><verse-line>before the body.</verse-line></verse-group><verse-group><verse-line>But this time—my death education— </verse-line><verse-line>locked in your leather skin you</verse-line></verse-group><verse-group><verse-line>watch me. Your scorched body </verse-line><verse-line>no longer in pain, your mind coherent.</verse-line></verse-group><verse-group><verse-line>Because this is how it happens </verse-line><verse-line>with burns—the body goes before the mind. I say</verse-line></verse-group><verse-group><verse-line><italic>You can’t survive this,</italic> and </verse-line><verse-line>in your answer came my death education:</verse-line></verse-group><verse-group><verse-line><italic>I know.</italic></verse-line></verse-group></sec></body></article>
